## Completion evidence
The isolated implementation supplies 36 original detailed multicolor SVGs for
29 operations and seven lifecycle states. The centered padded tile has no visible
header. Action names alone use bundled original Nunito at 600 weight and 10.01px:
ten percent larger than the first 9.1px compact design, still 23 percent below the
former 13px size. A static semantic border/halo follows work, document, caution,
error and completion states in both themes. Font-loading failures are explicit;
source and Windows packaging preserve the original SIL Open Font License 1.1.

Ruff, Black over 120 files, mypy over 74 modules and the full 932-test suite pass
before the final label-size refinement. After that refinement, all 83 GUI cases,
including every state at both compact/expanded sizes and both themes, pass with
focused Ruff/Black checks. Rendered pixels verify the border and actual halo;
font checks cover real family, weight and every stage-label glyph.

All 13 fictional screenshots and both walkthrough GIFs are regenerated after the
final size update. Directly inspect the final compact light and expanded dark
Run views; earlier complete state sheets establish distinct icon artwork. The
Run walkthrough has nine frames and the tutorial seven.

Publish exact reviewed source 6716546e23a27e0c0215bb99156b24fad9b4e32b and the
new immutable v0.2.4 tag. Main run 43037525084 and tag run 43037525101 both pass
hosted quality, Windows packaging and actual frozen offline smoke. The tag-gated
latest release is published at
https://github.com/Zanark/LinkedIn-EasyApply-Automaton/releases/tag/v0.2.4.
Independently verify its exact notes, source, downloaded ZIP, manifest,
checksums and all 454 archived files without extraction, execution or installation.
The prior v0.2.3 release remains unchanged.

At a verified source save point, coherently fast-forward original main, working
tree and index to that exact source. Original-source imports, version, the
unchanged launcher's nonlaunching check and 89 fictional GUI/resource cases pass.
Selected private/native metadata, all predecessor records and four independent
dashboard process creation identities remain intact. No installed application
is accessed, updated, launched or uninstalled; no real LinkedIn action, new live
qualification, fresh-machine execution or human acceptance is inferred.

